ice that ![](images/59/5914524b1d3db63c66998b75ca1d00a5dc4e294d2a8f10fe384d2b2ebf2af38e.svg) is a *type I* region. \nTo determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](images/39/39629b33e25aed05bf9a5ca36180f984e7ff8f863c6966d47f60483d672a8af4.png)\n\nSo, the region ![](images/59/5914524b1d3db63c66998b75ca1d00a5dc4e294d2a8f10fe384d2b2ebf2af38e.svg) can be defined as \n\n![](images/78/78cf2ea7f960497f7cc9beea602bf6ca0e82b74491f9f56cce76130d965d4a64.svg)\n\nNow, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n![](images/3c/3c423b0d423203621ab89258a6fff4cea190279b4dcc7170c8a7070bf1f85e24.svg)\n\nAnd that's our answer! Notice that, when we have a type I region, \n\n- the limits for ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg) are functions of ![](images/5a/5aac2c81021f3f9e468e7840c5f95ece35c10b894bdae19ec1d247bdeb47ac6f.svg)\n\n- the limits for ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg) are constants, and\n\n- we integrate over the variable ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg) before integrating over the variable ![](images/cf/cff7b257e3c71ec70dc7cd273bdd1cced4254993a43cffbfc338460c21bc7319.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186135088 #edb/ref 1065 4261 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186135088 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7c641021-bc5e-5b05-8a23-b198735ee5a3" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186135088 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186135089 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that we want to evaluate the repeated integral\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{x}^{2x} (x-2y) \\ \\mathrm{d}  y \\ \\mathrm{d}  x.\n$$\n\nNotice that the domain of integration is a type I region. \n\nTo compute this integral, we must bear the following important points in mind.\n\n- We start with the inner integral, as usual.\n\n- When integrating with respect to $y,$ we treat $x$ as though it were a constant.\n\n- The limits of integration for the inner integral are functions of $x.$ Once again, we treat $x$ as though it were a constant and substitute the integration limits as usual. After this step, there should be no more $y$'s in our integral.\n\n- Finally, we compute the outer integral.\n\nLet's apply these steps to solve the given problem.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{x}^{2x}(x-2y)\\text{ }dy]\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[xy-{y}^{2}]_{x}^{2x}\\text{ }dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[x\\cdot (2x)-{(2x)}^{2}]-[x\\cdot (x)-(x)^{2}]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[2{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}]-[{x}^{2}-{x}^{2}]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-2{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,dx & =-2{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{[{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}[{1}^{3}-{0}^{3}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186135089 #edb/ref 1065 4262 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186135089 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3698e7e3-4bc2-5db0-96b5-172131284b4a" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186135089 #edb/ref 1067 "Evaluating Repeated Integrals With Variable Limits" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321198 #edb/ref 1081 "-\\frac{11}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321198 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321198 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "04d2a009-9a40-5d25-99e2-4f97af963231" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321248 #edb/ref 1081 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321248 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321248 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "0b726bfa-ba4c-5d91-9f6d-6a3764d8755d" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321328 #edb/ref 1081 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321328 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321328 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "1594e17d-7011-5f7d-aa6a-12336ec25a8a" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321485 #edb/ref 1081 "-\\frac{1}{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321485 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321485 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "2b5f94c5-0d1b-5f79-944c-8cb9d821beed" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321496 #edb/ref 1081 "\\frac{6}{11}" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321496 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321496 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "2c533ee8-f9db-5f4a-a560-8035da471b44" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321596 #edb/ref 1081 "-\\frac{3}{11}" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321596 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321596 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "3a0552d2-cfa6-5c1e-901c-be3cad62fa64" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321834 #edb/ref 1081 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321834 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186321834 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "564621d9-f224-5fff-b159-cf3615e51a9b" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186322036 #edb/ref 1081 "\\frac{11}{6}" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186322036 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186322036 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "70ec84ef-6655-53bf-9eb0-7897a3753db2" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186322166 #edb/ref 1081 "\\frac{11}{12}" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186322166 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186322166 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "80d50f5a-f000-539b-a1db-5c8a13952505" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186322811 #edb/ref 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186322811 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186322811 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "d4f698ad-bda0-5b89-8175-c64721d84bac" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323315 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186321198 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323315 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186321496 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323315 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186321596 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323315 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186322036 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323315 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186322166 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323315 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323315 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323315 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186322166 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323315 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "4b2db87a-5385-53da-8e27-89a6fe772ff2" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186321248 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186321328 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186321485 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186321834 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186322811 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323483 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323483 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323483 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186321485 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323483 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "9eb45d35-7041-5bf4-8524-44adec58ddbf" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323935 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186323315 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323935 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37683" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323935 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323935 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate ${\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{x}^{1/x}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,dy\\,dx.$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323935 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "39356ac1-0a31-5e6e-9a6f-6a96bbbbe55c" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323935 #edb/ref 1074 "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{x}^{1/x}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{x}^{1/x}y\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{x}^{1/x}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2})dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}-1)\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}-1)\\,dx & =\\frac{1}{2}{[-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}-x]}_{1/2}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\frac{1}{3}+1-(\\frac{8}{3}+\\frac{1}{2})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{11}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323959 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186323483 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323959 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37865" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323959 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323959 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the double integral\n${∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{(1+x+y)^{2}}\\,dA,$\nwhere $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the line\n$y=1-x$ and the coordinate axes." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323959 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ad4a8e76-c297-5cff-8131-747df131b332" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186323959 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](images/95/95ebd0a4eb874972b459e53eecf1d57650f63284698fcad967c09620ac01cd99.png)\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I region.\n\n- The line $y=1-x$ intercepts the $x$-axis at $x=1.$\nSo, the $x$-limits are \n$0\\le x\\le 1.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](images/d0/d048f20f2299722cee598cc1005237627ecdd7643e996b269f26b5a096f01f2f.png)\n\nAs a result, the integral is defined over the following type I region: \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1-x}\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{(1+x+y)^{2}}\\,dA={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}\\frac{1}{(1+x+y)^{2}}\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}\\frac{1}{(1+x+y)^{2}}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{-x+1}\\frac{1}{(1+x+y)^{2}}\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-\\frac{1}{1+x+y}]}_{0}^{-x+1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-\\frac{1}{1+x+(1-x)}-(-\\frac{1}{1+x+0}))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{1+x})dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{1+x})dx & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x)]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-(0+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186348542 #edb/ref 1081 "e" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186348542 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186348542 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "0a7ddc79-cbfd-59b5-9638-d178b71104a6" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186349144 #edb/ref 1081 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186349144 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186349144 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "4b79160f-37ab-5192-8514-437d9b279188" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186349224 #edb/ref 1081 "\\frac{e}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186349224 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186349224 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "544819eb-b6d1-5a40-bb3a-d34d78eef696" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186349877 #edb/ref 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186349877 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186349877 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "a06fce6a-f06f-595a-9863-76102c8d8305" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186350556 #edb/ref 1081 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186350556 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186350556 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "f06aa1a1-4329-543e-8ec1-01bf70f9f867" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186350726 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186348542 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186350726 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186349144 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186350726 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186349224 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186350726 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186349877 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186350726 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186350556 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186350726 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186350726 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186350726 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186349877 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186350726 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "08077c01-ccff-5e05-a424-ef1243bb7696" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186351302 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186350726 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186351302 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81367" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186351302 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186351302 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the double integral\n${∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dA,$\nwhere $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the lines\n$x=e,$ $y=e$ and the curve $y={e}^{x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186351302 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b8f9d362-d296-527d-b3eb-8711496d6537" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186351302 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](images/aa/aa635ca5ef3198fea56d684b034de476a72e4ace2a4c51b37c6c59977036eb76.png)\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I region.\n\n- The line $y=e$ intercepts the curve $y={e}^{x}$ at $x=1.$\nSo, the $x$-limits are \n$1\\le x\\le e.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](images/b7/b78021a06c9fea100b75c66a619c425345cda3666d84da018895be15a53af06d.png)\n\nAs a result, the integral is defined over the following type I region: \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\,e\\le y\\le {e}^{x}}\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dA={\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{1}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{1}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}[{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{1}{y\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)]}_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{x})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}dx & ={[\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{2}]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡e}{2}-\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045585]}
